WEBVTT

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.190
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.860
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.990
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.240
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.790
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.290
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:34.130
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.300
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:41.140
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.060
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:48.610
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.530
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.530
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.950
Won't go away

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.790
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.920
We believed you

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:14.760
While we stand here

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.930
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:40.490
I'm not talking about the Great Japanese Empire.

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:43.290
Who thoughtlessly threw herself into this war.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:46.290
And I don't mean post-war Japan.

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:48.460
Who surrenders unconditionally, and is shamed.

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:51.340
After knowing both countries...

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.800
A new country has taken shape in my mind.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.730
Its name is Zipang.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:14.030
Zipang you say?

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.150
Yes, we'll call her that.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:20.570
That was the name the western travelers once used.

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:24.200
It's going to be a new country, however...

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.460
One that even the Japan of your era has not seen before.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:35.090
Zipang. I have no doubt that you can see it too.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:40.090
Collision!

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:44.310
The First Division US Marines' landing on Red Beach...

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:48.100
...is going to become a crucial point in history.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:52.560
This is their first campaign, and they lack reinforcements.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.610
If they're exterminated in one go...

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:57.320
...it would take a year to rebuild the unit.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:00.110
What's more, if 11000 soldiers are killed in battle...

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:04.530
...the US Military would be faced with intense pressure.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:08.540
Peace with honour is the first step to Zipang.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.250
It's essential that Japan consolidate her battlefront.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.250
But we want to avoid an unconditional surrender.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:18.260
And to do that, I've thought of a strategy!

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:22.550
And I'd like for the Mirai to fight alongside me!

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.770
What's going on?!

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:33.060
There've been crazy sounds coming out of this thing!

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.520
Some kind of powerful radio- waves must be causing this.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.150
- What did you say?
- General!

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:43.740
You have an emergency call from Admiral Turner.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:49.870
A fleet has been sighted, 30 km northeast of Red Beach.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.290
The Japanese?

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:57.090
General, this is what Sagittarius is after.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.210
After shaking our morale...

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:03.090
They make us pack up and retreat to our ships...

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.760
And then attack!

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.760
Rather than spending time and effort...

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:10.770
...preparing for a land battle, it would be...

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:15.310
...far more effective to take out the supply ships!

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.740
I've had it.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:24.860
We will not be manipulated by an invisible enemy!

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:28.240
I want our troops to spread further into the jungle!

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:31.330
Relay orders for anti-guerilla warfare!

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.330
Yes sir!

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:45.300
Commander Kadomatsu, the bombing will begin...

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.300
...in one minute.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.180
Depending on your decision...

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:51.680
I can still stall for time for you to retreat.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:55.440
Commander, there's a cave in the back of this place.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.320
We should move quickly!

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:03.440
Save your stubbornness for later!

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:07.780
Yosuke!

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:11.450
I don't know what fairytale your Zipang belongs to...

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:14.960
...but I don't like it!

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:21.420
You're playing your cards after seeing your opponent's hand.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.630
I do not have that luxury.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:28.430
Worst of all, I am furious with myself.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:30.470
For rescuing a man who's willing to cheat like this!

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:33.770
You had so many chances to turn back.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:39.480
On the Mirai... in Singapore... on the Toshinmaru.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:42.650
But I doubt that you've given it any thought.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:47.700
Do you really regret that I didn't?

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.370
Bring it on!

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:57.620
We will take you down along with the Yamato!

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.420
My party...

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:04.210
...absolutely will not pull out!

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:20.770
So you're really serious then?

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:24.690
I should be the one asking that!

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:27.740
Commander Kadomatsu, let me ask you this!

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:31.570
I have nothing to say to you!

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:36.000
As a commander entrusted with the lives of his subordinates...

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.210
Can you honestly say...

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:40.750
...that you're thinking clearly now?

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:46.840
I'm sure you can hear some crackling on the receiver.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:50.180
That's the sound of my brainwaves going wild.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:54.140
It's proof of how completely furious...

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:56.890
...I am at this moment!

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:00.810
I'm relieved to hear that!

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:03.060
What?!

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:06.070
Kusa-! Hold on! Kusaka!

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.620
- It's time.
- Yes.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:25.000
Admiral, message from the rear deck garage.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.800
It's an emergency call from Lieutenant Kusaka.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.720
We're in the middle of an operation!

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:31.680
What does he want?!

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.260
Let me talk to him.

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:43.310
The Mirai will fire at the Yamato?

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:48.280
So, what is your opinion on this?

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.150
My opinion is...

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.320
That they will not do anything to the Yamato.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.320
It's an intimidation tactic.

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:58.200
Meant to avoid war through a show of force.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:07:59.540
Their usual style.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:03.670
Yes. Their main objective has always been...

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:06.460
...to rescue human lives.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:10.800
Even if it costs the lives of 11000 US Marines...

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:14.050
the Mirai will aim to protect...

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:17.760
...the 2,500 men aboard Yamato.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.560
I do not believe that they will fire at us.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.810
This is purely a bluff.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:27.820
On the other hand, we don't have a guarantee.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.530
What I can guarantee, however...

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:31.190
...is the personality of the...

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.530
...commander of the landing party.

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:35.360
Commander Kadomatsu was furious with me.

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:40.540
Refused to retreat, and insisted on seeing his plan to the end.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:43.540
Worst case scenario...

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:48.340
The Mirai will fire at us out of anger.

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:52.090
I can confirm that after speaking with him directly.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:56.550
That man is the most composed person on this battlefield.

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:58.550
Very well.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.850
- Captain, let's begin.
- Yes!

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:10.520
Alright, I will proceed to the commander's room.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.070
Good.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.740
Fortune Inspector, did you hear that?

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:19.780
I heard everything. The negotiations had failed.

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:22.120
Kusaka's serious about it.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:24.830
The Yamato will carry out the attack.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:28.420
Captain, since it has come to this...

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:31.800
...our only choice is to launch Mirai's full Aegis System...

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.760
...at the Yamato to stop this war.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:40.180
Captain, we are dealing...

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:42.350
...with the infamous Isoroku Yamamoto.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:47.480
Yes. But it doesn't make a difference who the opponent is.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.270
Weapons Officer.

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:52.650
The only thing we need to be doing now...

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:54.530
...is fulfilling the Mirai's main objective.

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:57.320
All units stand by!

00:09:57.320 --> 00:10:01.160
Prepare for battle!

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:05.250
Track Number 1184.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.540
Combined Fleet's Flagship, Yamato!

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:10.250
I never thought the Mirai...

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:12.920
...would be Yamato's first opponent at sea.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:18.760
Captain, the Sea Sparrow can only handle 2 cannons.

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:21.350
The Yamato has nine barrels.

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:24.270
If they launch all 9 at once, we won't be able to fend them off.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:28.270
The difficulty also increases with the 2nd and 3rd rounds.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:32.520
So there's no way we can win with the cards we've got?

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:38.820
If we can block their first shot, we will have a shot at them.

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:41.530
Lieutenant, I'm counting on you.

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:44.080
Yes. We'll give it all we've got.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.290
First and Second Operators!

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:48.120
Watch for the moment of fire.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:51.460
If we can't catch the launch time, the auto won't start!

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:56.710
Illuminator Radar, stand by!

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:24.490
Cannons ready to fire!

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:28.500
It's finally time to prove that Yamato...

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:30.920
...is the most powerful ship in the world!

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:33.420
The Marines had better be prepared...

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:36.250
...for the power of 46 cm cannons.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:38.590
The Gods are on our side!

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:41.590
Commence attack! Fire!

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:45.010
Launch first shot!

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:46.600
Fire!

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:55.650
They've begun! The Yamato has fired!

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:57.320
How many?! Nine?!

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.190
No, only three.

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:01.610
15,000 to target!

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:04.240
Alright! Fire the sea sparrow! Now!

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:07.490
Rear Unit VLS Sea Sparrow to fire!

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:09.450
Salvo!

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:44.200
- Take cover! Hurry up!
- Yes!

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:48.660
Commander? Commander!

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:50.910
Take cover now!

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:53.460
I believe in him!

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:57.420
Masayuki won't miss!

00:12:58.500 --> 00:12:59.670
He's right.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:03.340
The Yamato cannons can only travel 780 yards per second.

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:05.430
The sea sparrow, travelling at 4,900 yards per second...

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:09.600
...shot out of the LRBM cannons of the Mirai...

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:11.560
...has a 100% chance of catching up to their shot.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:12.980
So what's the problem then?

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:17.730
The Sea Sparrow can only operate two cannons at a time.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:20.610
If they fire 3 cannons or more simultaneously...

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:23.490
I'm sure they'll think of something.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:26.360
I believe in Masayuki.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:30.240
Not a single shot from the Yamato will reach us!

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:38.170
The only way to intercept all 3 cannons...

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:41.710
...is to aim for the one in front, and set off the others behind it.

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:44.630
Sea Sparrow, reconfirm course!

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:45.470
Yes!

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:50.050
We cannot afford to be off by even a tenth of a second!

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:15.540
What's that?!

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:18.670
Retreat! Get all the men inside their camps!

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:20.630
Yes!

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:43.940
So that's what a 46cm gun is capable of.

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:45.820
I can feel it in my stomach.

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:49.490
Kusaka!

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:51.530
I won't let you get your way in this war.

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:54.330
No, I won't let you have your way in this world!

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:55.830
I swear that I'll stop you.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:58.080
Sea Sparrow. Bull's eye!

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:00.750
All targets have been destroyed.

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.420
Interception successful.

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:15.260
What? Still 4 seconds to impact?!

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:17.390
Scout! What's happening!?

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:21.400
Sir! None of the bombs have reached Guadalcanal Island.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:23.520
They've all exploded in midair!

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:25.610
In midair?

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:28.280
Were they faulty rounds? Was it lightning?

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.700
And don't tell me...

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:33.490
...that the cannons hit someone else's plane by accident!

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:35.580
All three cannons?

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:38.620
Ridiculous! That's just not possible!

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:40.620
We have a message from the Mirai!

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:42.330
Really? Read it out.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.790
Yes! Right away!

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:50.090
Our ship has intercepted all the shots fired by your ship.

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:54.640
We're fully equipped against your attacks.

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:57.310
Intercepted? What does that mean?

00:15:57.310 --> 00:16:01.350
You mean they fired at the shots that we fired?!

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:06.060
We request that your ship cease your attacks immediately.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.980
We have several cannons prepared...

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:10.900
They weigh 454 kilograms each...

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:13.070
...and can easily cover a distance of...

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:17.200
...more than 270 miles.

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:18.580
That's all.

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:22.960
A shooting range of more than 270 miles?!

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:35.430
It was worth the effort, to have gone this far.

00:16:56.370 --> 00:17:01.160
So, you're finally bearing your fangs, Mirai.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:06.880
Commander Kadomatsu, and the Mirai itself have changed.

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:11.210
It's proof that they're not gods, but humans.

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:14.970
Nonetheless, this war is not meaningless.

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:19.220
This will be a ritual purification...

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.770
...for the Imperial Japanese Navy!

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:45.120
Report!

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:48.420
No casualties sustained from the bombardment!

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:51.460
The cannons were fired from the east.

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:53.710
But the Arrow of Sagittarius from the west.

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:58.640
What's this demonstration supposed to mean?!

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:02.140
In my 30 years in the army...

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:06.600
I have never once experienced anything like this.

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:12.570
Isn't there anyone among the Allied Forces...

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.990
...who can understand what's going on?

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:19.410
All crew on standby mode!

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:21.990
All crew on standby mode!

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:26.330
Attention! I will explain the situation.

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:31.340
We successfully intercepted all of the Yamato's cannons.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.960
The landing party, headed by Commander Kadomatsu...

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:37.630
...is safe and sound.

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:41.140
We will continue to maintain a state of battle!

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:43.680
All units, be alert! That's all!

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:47.480
Yamato.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.490
I'm coming in.

00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:01.410
You didn't have any appetite for breakfast...

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:03.370
...so I brought you some coffee instead.

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:12.630
Where is the palace?

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:16.210
Palace? Oh, the Imperial Palace?

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:18.510
I don't know. I'm sorry but...

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:19.800
...I'm quite bad with directions.

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:24.850
I'd have to go consult the CIC. But... I mean...

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:27.060
What are you doing?

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:31.100
This ship has entered into battle with the Yamato, correct?

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:34.190
Thus...

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:37.030
I am now a prisoner of war.

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:39.070
And...

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:41.610
...as soldier of the Imperial Navy...

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:44.990
...I have only one option.

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:48.410
- No! Wait!
- Stay away from me!

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:25.490
All cannon vaults ready!

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:37.540
I'll show you!

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:42.720
The Yamato doesn't back down from a threat by a single ship!

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:54.730
Admiral Yamamoto.

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:59.650
I request an immediate halt to the operation.

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:01.690
Halt to the operation?

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:05.410
Do you really understand...

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:08.740
...what it means to back down from this?

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:12.750
This isn't just any ship. It's the Yamato.

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:16.330
Aside from being the biggest and strongest in the world.

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:19.920
It's also a symbol of the Imperial Navy.

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:25.380
The Mirai does not want to fight the Yamato.

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:27.800
Are you saying that the Mirai isn't an enemy...

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:30.060
...even after intercepting our attack?

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:33.850
They do not mean to enter into battle with us.

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:36.770
Their sole aim is the preservation of life.

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:40.650
There's no point in fighting someone who isn't the enemy.

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:43.570
I don't consider this a defeat.

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:49.410
After the battle at Midway...

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:53.540
Are you asking our Imperial Navy...

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:57.500
...to suffer another humiliation?

00:21:57.500 --> 00:21:59.460
Lieutenant Kusaka?

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:17.110
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.250 --> 00:22:22.350
Just peacefully

00:22:21.820 --> 00:22:34.130
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.270 --> 00:22:47.040
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.550 --> 00:22:53.650
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.220 --> 00:22:59.720
I kept on praying

00:23:01.130 --> 00:23:11.540
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.400 --> 00:23:27.250
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:40.800 --> 00:23:42.850
The sea sparrow will exhaust its cannons in minutes.

00:23:43.350 --> 00:23:44.350
We'll have to rely on the...

00:23:44.810 --> 00:23:46.350
...Tomahawk to destroy the source of the attack.

00:23:46.600 --> 00:23:48.180
Message to Yamato:

00:23:48.180 --> 00:23:50.350
I am looking forward to your cooperation.

00:23:50.690 --> 00:23:52.400
I am a pathetic man.

00:23:52.400 --> 00:23:54.860
As a soldier, I must do all I can for my country!

00:23:55.360 --> 00:23:58.360
Everything we know is only a pile of records.

00:23:58.360 --> 00:23:59.820
They don't tell us about the real Isoroku Yamamoto.

00:23:59.900 --> 00:24:04.870
Next Episode:  The Living and the Dead

00:24:00.860 --> 00:24:02.950
When we're given an order...

00:24:02.950 --> 00:24:04.530
We will execute it.

00:24:04.870 --> 00:24:09.870
This story is purely fiction. The names of the
characters and organizations that appear have no
connections with actual people and organizations.
